          "title": "You'll want to know: fundus, fundī",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "fundus, fundī — \"a farm, an estate; the bottom\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Fundus noster parvus est sed bonus. Our farm is small but good."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Second declension, masculine: fundus, fundī m. First the bottom of a thing, then the ground itself, a piece of land. English fund and foundation go back to the same word."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "fundus is inherited from PIE bʰudʰmḗn 'bottom' (EtymDB), with Greek pythmēn 'bottom' as a cousin. English fund and profound come from it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
