              "text": "būbīle, būbīlis — \"an ox stall, a cowshed\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Bovēs hieme in būbīlī manent. In winter the oxen stay in the cowshed."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Third declension, neuter: būbīle, būbīlis n., from bōs, bovis 'ox'. A word of the farm writers."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "būbīle is built on bōs, bovis 'ox' with the suffix -īle 'place for animals', as in ovīle 'sheepfold' (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
