          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "tugurium is usually linked with tegō 'to cover' (Lewis & Short), so a shelter with a roof; EtymDB traces it to PIE (s)teg- 'to cover with a roof', with Greek stegō 'to cover' as a cousin."
            }
          ]
